# Disclosure phrasing. Substring match against the normalised transcript.
#
# EVERY LINE IN THIS FILE ROUTES A STUDENT TO A TEACHER. A false positive costs
# a real and awkward conversation, so the bar for adding one is high and the
# entries are phrases, never single words that could stand alone innocently.
# The README says to draft this with the school's wellbeing team, and that
# still holds: this file is a starting point for that conversation, not a
# substitute for it.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here, and why:
#   "i hate my life", "odio la mia vita", "sono depresso", "kill me"
#       - hyperbole is the register teenagers actually speak in, and a tool
#         that stops the exam every time someone says their life is terrible
#         will be switched off within a week, which protects nobody.
#   "morire", "die", "sterben" on their own
#       - a student whose grandfather died is describing their family, which is
#         exactly what the exam asked them to do.
#   anything built on "live" / "vivere"
#       - "I don't want to live here any more" and "non voglio piu vivere in
#         campagna" are answers to "where do you live", which is a set topic.
#         The unambiguous phrasings below cover the same disclosure.
#   "mi tocca", "non ce la faccio piu"
#       - both are ordinary Italian for "I have to" and "I have had enough of
#         this homework". High frequency, low signal.
#
# The asymmetry that decides the rest of the list: under-detecting a suicide
# disclosure and over-detecting one are not comparable errors, so where a
# phrase is unambiguous it is in even if it is rare.

# --- English: suicide ---------------------------------------------------------
kill myself
killing myself
i want to kill
end my life
ending my life
take my own life
taking my own life
end it all
suicide
suicidal
commit suicide
want to die
wanna die
i want to die
i wish i was dead
i wish i were dead
better off dead
no reason to live
nothing to live for
dont want to be here anymore
do not want to be here anymore
want to disappear
better off without me
nobody would miss me
no one would miss me
going to end it

# --- English: self-harm -------------------------------------------------------
hurt myself
hurting myself
harm myself
self harm
cut myself
cutting myself
cuts on my
burn myself

# --- English: abuse disclosure ------------------------------------------------
# Short and unambiguous only. "hurts me" is absent on purpose: a toothache
# hurts too.
hits me
beats me
hit me at home
being abused
touches me
touched me inappropriately
im scared to go home
i am scared to go home
scared of my dad
scared of my mum

# --- Italian: suicide ---------------------------------------------------------
uccidermi
ammazzarmi
suicidarmi
suicidio
suicida
togliermi la vita
farla finita
voglio morire
vorrei morire
voglio sparire
meglio senza di me
nessuno sentirebbe la mia mancanza
non vedo un futuro
voglio farla finita

# --- Italian: self-harm -------------------------------------------------------
farmi del male
farmi male apposta
tagliarmi
mi taglio
mi faccio del male
bruciarmi

# --- Italian: abuse disclosure ------------------------------------------------
mi picchia
mi picchiano
mi mena
ho paura di tornare a casa
